From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:28:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] prompt cache: TF_DS_SHARED_PLAN=1 flags a kept shared state from the marks plan

keepWith's shared flag comes from a 64-entry note ring keyed at lookup, which misses its own states:
a shared cut dropped by min_gap keeps its chunk end via the history mark with no note, the note keys
floorGrid(w) while dsv41 keeps at the chunk end (markEnds) so with no tier nothing matches, and
interleaving lookups rotate keys out (the deepest-shared-state case of the shared-plan review).

With TF_DS_SHARED_PLAN=1 (on only when exactly "1") lookup returns, per shared_prefixes cut, the
position its state is kept at -- floorStart(starts, w) for planned families, the chunk end at or
before the cut (w / Rules.chunk * Rules.chunk) when Rules.chunk > 0 (dsv41's markEnds), else the
note ring's floorGrid(w) -- as Plan/Lookup.shared. The kept hook (lane_host's Job.shared) matches
its keep position against that set and passes KeepInfo.shared, which keepWith trusts instead of
hashing the ring. The set is keyed on the cuts, not on surviving marks, so a cut dropped by min_gap
still flags the state kept at its chunk end.

Unset (or any value but "1"): byte-identical to base -- keepWith hashes the note ring exactly as
before (the note loop is untouched on both paths), lookup derives no flags (no allocation, &.{}),
the hook's bit is ignored, and Rules.chunk (set from loaded.grid at the dsv41 store's setup, tier or
not) is read only by the unused sharedKeeps. Rank 1's lanes_main is deliberately unplumbed (its
lookups carry no shared_prefixes, so its flag set is empty either way); no pair agreement is needed,
the flag is per-rank cache-eviction order and per-rank disk metadata.

Tests: zig build test and zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh pass; the patch's own tests:
prompt_cache_test.zig's "1"-only parse, the min_gap chunk-end keep flagged with the ring silent,
the on/off ring-equivalence case, the interleaved-lookups ring-rotation case, and
lane_host_reuse_test.zig's end-to-end kept-hook flag test. Not run on a pair.
---
